'''Yekora''' is a [[Papuan languages|Papuan language]] spoken in [[Morobe Province]], [[Papua New Guinea]]. It is part of the Binandere family of the [[Trans–New Guinea languages|Trans–New Guinea]] phylum of languages, and is particularly close to [[Zia language|Zia]].

